{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 names a specific inherited variable — the isomorphism-revealing confrontation that translation enables — but its refutation condition (a lineage achieving confrontation without translating into a rival vocabulary) does not actually test the inheritance. The condition challenges dependence on translation, but it never tests whether the inherited variable itself is the confrontation as opposed to any other productive output of translation (e.g., vocabulary enrichment, analogy generation). A lineage could satisfy the refutation by achieving isomorphism-revealing confrontation via direct structural comparison without a rival-vocabulary translation, yet this would show only that translation is not the unique route to confrontation; the sharpening claim — that confrontation rather than translation is the operative causal variable — is still not independently falsified. The refutation thus severs dependence but leaves the inheritance assertion untouched: the target conflates refuting a prerequisite with refuting an inherited differentiator.","counterexample":["Suppose a lineage discovers isomorphism between two problem domains purely by aligning their graph-theoretic structure, with no translation step into a rival vocabulary. SRC_001's stated refutation fires, dependence on SRC_002 is broken. Yet the claim that the operative inherited variable is 'confrontation, not translation' is entirely consistent with this counterexample — the lineage still achieved confrontation — so the inheritance/sharpening claim survives its own stated refutation condition."],"target":"39ff5d4dc1f0baf28b656b3f7a4daeab146d539dc9a8dd41039ee9294a8fd9f5"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 frames the neighbourhood incompatibility as a relation between SRC_002 and SRC_004, then asserts that SRC_004 reduces to SRC_002 iff P-tractability implies Q-unification. But a conditional reduction (A reduces to B iff P→Q) is not a substantive reduction claim; it is a tautological restatement of the incompatibility the target already described. The problem context requires naming a substantive relation kind and stating what it is refuted if. Here the 'reduction' is entirely hostage to an unestablished implication, so the target asserts no actual dependence, reduction, or integration between the artifacts — only a logical conditional whose truth value is left open. The target therefore fails to propose a genuine relation: it restates the endpoints' threshold mismatch under a reduction label, which the problem context explicitly excludes ('a summary of the endpoints is not a relation').","counterexample":["If P-tractability does not imply Q-unification (which the target itself concedes is the open question), then no reduction of SRC_004 to SRC_002 is asserted, and if it does, the reduction is merely definitional rather than mechanistic. In neither branch does the target commit to a substantive relation holding across the neighbourhood."],"target":"cee4e5a19c9cfef8b8ef0d11cbadd92ae3afd611d113cba690ddb294085847db"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"ff738ae88dbb5ca1bb303654bba539f9e9c693514337d90f25ce17922a3f4209"}]}